timeline it's  actually kind of interesting as moon  knight writer jeremy slater doesn't  exactly know where it falls on the mcu  timeline and apparently that was  actually done very intentionally they  did it on purpose but here's what he  said a lot of people have asked this but  i have no idea sorry we didn't know when  our show would debut in relation to  their other shows and films so the  timeline was intentionally left vague  that's very interesting because moon  knight does kind of seem to be a show  that is very separate from the mcu yes  of course it takes place inside of the  mcu but there aren't really many  connections to the mcu and other  superheroes so it would make sense that  they weren't really trying to connect it  to anything and put it any specific  place in the timeline however like i  said there is an easter egg that does  give us a pretty specific time frame now  this easter egg was found by ryan over  at screencrush so credit to him for this  it's in moon night episode 1 where  steven is trying to stay awake and he's  learning about the egyptian inead well  when stephen is reading up on the ini ad  we can actually see some other books in  the background and they are about asgard  and wakanda however the asgard book  seems to be specifically about new  asgard on the bottom the book appears to  read the history of wakanda but on the  top it seems to read what's old is new  again asgard now we actually know enough  about thor love and thunder from the  merchandising that has been released to  know that after avengers in-game new  asgard is now on earth and they're kind  of an attraction now for the people of  earth and kind of a vacation location  and we know that they do such things as  asgard boat tours and we'll talk about  this in just a minute but what this  really is pointing to is the fact that  asgard being new again as in being on  earth means that moon night most likely  takes place after new asgard is on earth  a lot of people have 