 really interesting is this easter egg  right here the book about asgard and the  book about wakanda and they're  interesting for two reasons as there are  two different books the wakanda easter  egg is very very interesting because of  all the events that are taking place in  moon night in marvel comics the black  panther god bast is a part of the  egyptian iniad and in episode 3 we even  see a statue of bast however the avatar  for bast is not in the meeting and i'm  trying to be vague to avoid spoilers for  those who haven't seen it but stephen  explains that there are nine egyptian  gods in the inead in the mcu and there  were not nine gods in attendance which  means there are some gods missing and  one of those gods missing was the black  panther and egyptian god bast and this  is very interesting and it also does  kind of help the timeline question as  well but what's interesting about bast  being gone and the avatar not being  there is that black panther 2 wakanda  forever is coming out this year as well  and reports have actually said that we  will be seen best again in wakanda  forever this could explain why we didn't  see the avatar of bast in episode 3. the  gods were called together but bast  wasn't there what was bast doing well  probably dealing with whatever is  happening in wakanda forever we know  that bast actually chose the very first  black panther and guided him to the  heart-shaped herb and we know that a new  black panther is going to have to come  in wakanda forever it would make sense  that bast would be a part of this and  this is a sad subject but although we  don't know for sure yet if they're going  to kill t'challa in the film since  chadwick boseman is no longer with us we  do assume that he is going to be dead in  the mcu and rumors of a funeral scene  have been going on so perhaps bast  couldn't make it because she was  attending the funeral of t'challa the  black panther and again this would mean  that moon knight takes place around  wakanda forever if bast truly isn't  there because she is dealing with  wakanda forever events which means this  show probably takes place like i said  between three months to a year after  avengers in game and it's really  interesting that all of the stuff that  we've seen so far for thor love and  thunder shows us that new asgard is kind  of going to be a tourist attraction now  but this makes sense because they're not  rich anymore they don't have a city of  gold anymore on asgard there on earth  now and it looks like they're gonna have  to be making some money to survive but  we'll have to wait and see on that  fortunately we don't have to wait that  much longer for thor love and thunder in  the meantime let me know what you think  about these easter eggs and when moon  night takes place in the mcu timeline  and its connection to black panther  wakanda forever let me know in the  comments down below don't forget to like  the video and subscribe so you don't  miss out on any of the latest mcu news  for live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter and as always  thank you all so much for watching woof  [Music]
 

